# Line endings.
#
# Why this file exists: the working tree on this machine is Windows and its text
# files use CRLF, while Git stores LF. Without the attributes below, `git status`
# reports dozens of files as modified even though their content is byte-identical
# once the line endings are normalised — a comparison against the published
# repository found 49 such files and 0 genuine differences.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text, normalise it to LF in the repository,
# and — because that normalisation also applies when Git compares the working
# tree — stop the false "modified" reports. Checking out still produces the
# platform's native endings where no `eol` is given.

* text=auto

# The files the CI reads and renders. Pinned to LF in the working tree as well,
# so that a checkout on Windows cannot reintroduce CRLF into the manuscript,
# the configuration, the registers or the bibliography.
*.qmd    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf
*.bib    text eol=lf
*.csl    text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf

# Assets and build products. Never convert, never diff.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.epub   binary
*.pyc    binary
